add_claim("THE INTERACTION THAT MAKES THE SELECTIVE SET WORK: playing the International and Allstar cups means 'you have to win 11 or 13 matches in legendary division! **so, you can skip 2 away games**' - whereas skipping those cups makes the third objective '**win all legendary games or never get defeated in legendary division**', forcing all 15. So the cup route is what buys the league skip.", 3, "career/cups-buy-the-league-skip", [e_cg])
add_claim("THE CONCEDE-WITHOUT-PLAYING TACTIC, which is what makes the selective set fast: 'After winning 9-10 games or making sure we're gonna win the legendary division I just **matches finish without playing and lose** as even after losing we get around **150 75+75 coins from home games** and this is without investing any time. Ya I do lose 10 gems of win all games objective but this way I save time and can start a new season again.' **So the coin income survives a conceded match; only the win-all objective does not.**", 3, "career/concede-without-playing", [e_cg], notes="Turns the corpus's home-only farming rule into a time-efficient routine")
add_claim("THE PER-COMPETITION GEM BREAKDOWN: **30 gems for the Legendary Division · 25 for the Diamond Cup · 15 for the Global Challenge Cup · 5 for the allstar match · 20 for the International Cup · 15 for the International Allstars.** That is the table behind the 4+ rule, and it explains the GCC exclusion - 'the matches are way too many' for 15 gems.", 3, "career/per-competition-gem-breakdown", [e_cg])
add_claim("THE PROMOTION MECHANICS: promotion requires the **Division Objectives**, found in **My Club**, completed within **15 Division Games** - 'failing which you are denied a promotion and have to repeat that Division.' The objectives demand both a finishing position and a **goal count**, and 'out of 15 Division games, even if you manage to win **10 games**, you will end up being the table topper. **What's more challenging is the goal count.**'", 2, "career/promotion-objectives-mechanics", [e_cg])
add_claim("THE CUP-DIVISION LOCK: 'U can only win Elite Division cup in Elite Division, Gold cup as well. **Once u're promoted to another league, Gold cup becomes Diamond cup**' - so a lower cup is not farmable after promotion. The cup route is a one-shot per division, not a repeatable farm.", 3, "career/cup-division-lock", [e_cg])
add_claim("THE 80-OVR DEFENDER ROUTE, a higher-yield alternative to the Common-coach loop: 'you should buy **gold 80 overall rated defenders**. Afterward, **sell them and you will receive 1 rare coach**. The reason you should buy defenders specifically is that they are the least expensive outfield player. The cheapest of course being goalkeepers.'", 3, "coaching/80-ovr-defender-to-rare-coach", [e_cg])
add_claim("THE F2P GEM FLOOR: 'If you find yourself struggling to acquire gems, complete the daily challenge tasks for **8 gems a day**' - about 240 gems a month from challenges alone, before any DLL or clan income.", 3, "economy/daily-challenges-8-gems", [e_cg])
add_claim("SCOUT COSTS: a **Common scout is 75 coins**, a **Legendary scout 500 coins** - which is the arithmetic behind the corpus's recommendation to hire Commons and let the probability ladder do the work.", 3, "transfers/scout-costs-75-and-500", [e_cg])
add_claim("THE CLAN REWARD LADDER, with thresholds: **25,000 clan points to unlock anything at all**, then **25 gems at 1,000,000**, a Legendary XP boost at 2,000,000, a Legendary Scout at 3,000,000, 500 coins at 5,000,000, a Rare Special Coach at 7,500,000, and **150 gems at 10,000,000**. The 25-gem and 150-gem tiers are independently corroborated ('25 Gems + 150 Gems (10,000,000 Clan Points Needed to unlock) = 175'); the middle tiers are single-source from a source rejected for tables.", 3, "clans/reward-ladder-thresholds", [e_cg], notes="Middle tiers flagged single-source; the endpoints are two-source")
add_claim("THE PER-MATCH CLAN RATE: 'Recibes aproximadamente **3.5k Puntos de Clan por ganar un partido online**' - about 3,500 clan points per online win. So the corpus's 350,000 personal cap is roughly **100 online wins**, which is the real size of the clan contribution you can make.", 3, "clans/3500-points-per-online-win", [e_cg])
add_claim("THE 50-GEM IN-CLAN PRIZE, and what the cap actually does: 'Cualquier otra cosa que ganes te va a ayudar a ser el primero en tu clan y a obtener las **50 gemas** al final de la temporada, pero no va a ayudar a los puntos totales de tu clan.' **So past 350k you are only racing your own clanmates for 50 gems** - the clan's total no longer moves, which is the whole reason clan choice is competitive rather than social.", 3, "clans/past-the-cap-you-race-your-clanmates", [e_cg])
add_claim("THE CLAN RECRUITMENT MARKET'S EXPECTATIONS, which is what makes clan choice competitive: members advertise '**200k minimum each season**', '350k clan points this season' and '700K points per season', while clans advertise targets of '**8 million season prize**' and '7.5m points each season'. A leader reports expelling anyone contributing under **20,000 points in their first hour**; another with 145 million collective points 'just expell anyone that doesn't perform or is inactive for a week.'", 3, "clans/recruitment-market-expectations", [e_cg])
